    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0766" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg670"/>

                <head>No. 464.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brown to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 18, 1872</date>.
                        (Received February 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy and
                    translation of a communication received from the Sublime Porte on the subject of
                    the commerce of Turkish tobacco.</p>
                <p>The system proposed by the government, of an excise character, is a new one for
                    this country, and will have an important influence on this branch of the
                    commerce of some countries, in the article of tobacco produced in this empire. I
                    believe there is very little exported to the United States, and yet the subject
                    is one of interest to the mercantile community in general.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN P. BROWN.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d463-a1.xml" xpointer="d463-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
